 That hard limit is `superchat-agent-max-tool-calls`, 120 calls per execution. While an execution runs, the status line shows `tools N/120`. When 15 calls are left (after the 105th of 120; `superchat-tool-budget-reminder-left`, nil turns it off) the model is told so once. Calls past the limit are refused, and the execution's end says so: the chat, `M-x superchat-pending` and the notices list read `Cut off after 120 tool calls`, and the ending facts carry `:tool-budget (:action cut-off :limit 120 :used 120)`. When `superchat-tool-failure-brake` (default 3, nil turns it off) tool calls in a row have failed, the execution stops: no further call and no further request, and the chat, `M-x superchat-pending` and the notices list read `Stopped after 3 failed calls in a row`. A call that succeeds starts the count again, and a call you or the permission level refused is not a failure. The brake is one of `superchat-tool-loop-hooks`: functions asked about every tool call before its body and after its result, which may let it be, give the model other text (the original stays on the Tape, the rewrite is recorded as `tool.rewritten`), or stop the execution. nil turns them all off. An `edit_buffer` error (text not found, more than one match) counts as a failed call, like an `eval_elisp` error.
 
+When the provider says a reply was cut off at the output limit (stop reason `length`), none of that reply's tool calls runs (`superchat-cut-off-reply-runs-nothing`, default t, nil runs them as before). The model is told `Your reply was cut off at the output limit (N tokens), so none of its tool calls ran. Do the same work in smaller pieces: …` and asked again; after `superchat-llm-unknown-tool-retries` (2) such retries in a row the execution stops, and the chat, `M-x superchat-pending` and the notices list read `Stopped: the reply was cut off at the output limit 3 times in a row`. A reply of text only that was cut off is still the answer, with a line under it saying so. Every cut-off is the fact `response.cut-off` on the Tape, with the option off too. Without a stop reason from the provider nothing changes; nothing is guessed from the text.
+
 **Memory not persisting**
 
 Check `superchat-data-directory` and that the SQLite database is writable. Run `/recall test` to verify queries work. Memory auto-retrieval only activates for queries longer than 8 characters (configurable via `superchat-memory-auto-recall-min-length`).
