+
+Slice 12b (`reports/guidance-2026-10-11/SLICE-12.md`). A reply whose stop reason is `length` runs none of its calls (`superchat-cut-off-reply-runs-nothing`); the model is told the limit and asked for smaller pieces; after `superchat-llm-unknown-tool-retries` retries in a row the execution stops with the reason on its ending, under the answer and on the pending row. Every cut-off is the fact `response.cut-off`. A text-only reply cut off stays the answer, with a line under it. Without streaming, the stop reason of a reply whose arguments did not parse is kept for the error callback. Tests: `scripts/reply-cut-off-regression.el`. Not covered: Claude `stop_reason`, OpenAI Responses `incomplete_details`. Not done with the slice-11b per-call hooks: they run per call after llm.el has added the assistant record, while a cut-off must refuse the whole reply before its first call. The DeepSeek streaming handler change lives only in the user's llm fork working tree (`slice-12-llm-deepseek-stop-reason.diff`), not in this repository.
+
 ### Open observation: a rewrite is seen by the model only in that execution (2026-10-20, recorded, not ruled)
 
